"45,0": {
"v": "\nSPRI clean-up protocol:\n\n*allow beads to sit in RT for 30 mins prior. Ensure you have enough 80% ethanol.\n\n1. Add room temperature beads to rxn. Mix well by pipetting up and down 10 times.\n2. Incubate for 5 mins at room temperature.\n3. Place samples on magnetic rack, and incubate for 5 mins on the rack.\n4. Remove supernatant and add 200uL of 80% EtOH to samples while on the magnetic rack. \n5. Incubate at room temperature for 30s and remove the supernatant.\n6. Repeat EtOH wash step once for a total of 2 washes.\n7. Air dry the beads for 5 mins while on the magnetic rack.\n8. Remove tube from magnetic rack. Elute DNA from beads into nuclease free water (can also use 0.1x TE Buffer, 10mM Tris-HCl)\n9. Pipette mix and incubate for 2 mins at room temperature off the magnetic rack.\n10. Place on magnetic rack until solution is clear, ~ 5 mins.\n11. Aspirate supernatant and transfer to a clean nuclease free PCR tube.\n\n**Checkpoint: Samples can be stored frozen at -20 \u00b0C and library prep resumed the next day.\n"
},
